00:21:48.068 --> 00:21:49.610
Because what's going
to happen in GKE

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:50.600
is it's just going
to figure it out,

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:51.410
and it's going to give you one.

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:52.040
It's going to fake it.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:52.590
No problem.

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:53.610
It's all taken care of.

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:56.000
GKE On-Prem, you've got to
be a little more specific.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:21:57.390
That's where the F5 comes in.

00:21:57.390 --> 00:22:00.650
That's where you have to say,
oh, use this IP from my F5

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:02.240
I've preallocated.

00:22:02.240 --> 00:22:03.950
So I can't do it
exactly like this.

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:06.810
But don't worry, I've
got it all figured out.

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:08.300
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:09.967
I don't think I have
