00:34:20.980 --> 00:34:24.440
The important part here-- and
it's really what Matt showed

00:34:24.440 --> 00:34:26.145
before in the early slides--

00:34:26.145 --> 00:34:27.770
the reason why we're
looking into this,

00:34:27.770 --> 00:34:29.540
and it's the
jurisdictional reason.

00:34:29.540 --> 00:34:33.100
That's our main one.

00:34:33.100 --> 00:34:38.688
NetEnt has about 28
licenses across our markets.

00:34:38.688 --> 00:34:40.870
And the gambling
industries is sort

00:34:40.870 --> 00:34:45.370
of going through a pretty fast
reregulation, I would say.

00:34:45.370 --> 00:34:49.460
Regulators, however, are not the
most modern people right now.

00:34:49.460 --> 00:34:55.750
So going cloud is not something
that we can do in all places,

00:34:55.750 --> 00:34:58.420
until last year pretty
much, because then we

00:34:58.420 --> 00:35:01.300
saw a pretty big shift in
some of the regulators.

00:35:01.300 --> 00:35:07.060
So cloud is more
and more OK to use.

00:35:07.060 --> 00:35:09.640
The problem for us then
was that it was only some.

00:35:09.640 --> 00:35:12.860
So if we were to
cloud at that point,

00:35:12.860 --> 00:35:14.500
we would end up in
that position where

00:35:14.500 --> 00:35:19.180
you have on-prem that looks in
one way and then going cloud

00:35:19.180 --> 00:35:21.530
looks a completely
different way.

00:35:21.530 --> 00:35:23.530
And with regard
to our complexity,

00:35:23.530 --> 00:35:26.092
I'm going to go through that
a little bit more later on.

00:35:26.092 --> 00:35:28.300
We kind of said that we
don't want to take that path.

00:35:28.300 --> 00:35:29.342
We're not ready for that.

00:35:29.342 --> 00:35:31.790
We can't add yet another
layer of complexity.

00:35:31.790 --> 00:35:36.710
